{"id":"bd10b20ea87ceba0","group":"27","path":"27/27-thm-readoncecertificate.md","title":"A pair of prime supports certifies failure of positive read-once","display":"thm-readoncecertificate — A pair of prime supports certifies failure of positive read-once","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Boolean Functions: Theory, Algorithms, and Applications","book_abbrev":"27","label":"27-thm-readoncecertificate","aliases":["27-thm-readoncecertificate"],"display":"thm-readoncecertificate — A pair of prime supports certifies failure of positive read-once","depends_on":["[[27-df-minmaxsupport]]","[[27-thm-gurvich]]"],"source_file":"C:/Users/lzy/Documents/BaiduSyncdisk/calibre/Yves Crama, Peter L. Hammer/Boolean Functions_ Theory, Algorith (5073)/Boolean Functions_ Theory, Algo - Yves Crama, Peter L. Hammer.pdf","source_section":"§10.5 Theorem 10.9 membership proof","source_printed_pages":"472","source_pdf_pages":"496","verification_status":"source-certificate-and-verification-proof-checked"},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Boolean Functions: Theory, Algorithms, and Applications"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"27"},{"key":"label","html":"27-thm-readoncecertificate"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>27-thm-readoncecertificate</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-readoncecertificate — A pair of prime supports certifies failure of positive read-once"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"a38b86e606184c7f\" href=\"?note=a38b86e606184c7f\" title=\"27-df-minmaxsupport\">27-df-minmaxsupport</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"2258152dd7a3f9d8\" href=\"?note=2258152dd7a3f9d8\" title=\"27-thm-gurvich\">27-thm-gurvich</a></span></div>"},{"key":"source_file","html":"C:/Users/lzy/Documents/BaiduSyncdisk/calibre/Yves Crama, Peter L. Hammer/Boolean Functions_ Theory, Algorith (5073)/Boolean Functions_ Theory, Algo - Yves Crama, Peter L. Hammer.pdf"},{"key":"source_section","html":"§10.5 Theorem 10.9 membership proof"},{"key":"source_printed_pages","html":"472"},{"key":"source_pdf_pages","html":"496"},{"key":"verification_status","html":"source-certificate-and-verification-proof-checked"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\\in\\mathbb Z_{\\ge0}\">\\(n\\in\\mathbb Z_{\\ge0}\\)</span>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"f\\in\\mathrm{Monotone}_n\">\\(f\\in\\mathrm{Monotone}_n\\)</span>；<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\chi_S,\\mathcal M(f),\\mathcal X(f)\">\\(\\chi_S,\\mathcal M(f),\\mathcal X(f)\\)</span> 见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"a38b86e606184c7f\" href=\"?note=a38b86e606184c7f\" title=\"27-df-minmaxsupport\">27-df-minmaxsupport</a>，<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ReadOnceFunc}_n\">\\(\\mathrm{ReadOnceFunc}_n\\)</span> 与 Gurvich 判据见 <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"2258152dd7a3f9d8\" href=\"?note=2258152dd7a3f9d8\" title=\"27-thm-gurvich\">27-thm-gurvich</a>。<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"A,B\\subseteq[n]\">\\(A,B\\subseteq[n]\\)</span>。</p>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"A\\in\\mathcal M(f)\\Longleftrightarrow\n\\left(f(\\chi_A)=1\\land\\forall i\\in A\\;(f(\\chi_{A\\setminus\\{i\\}})=0)\\right).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[A\\in\\mathcal M(f)\\Longleftrightarrow\n\\left(f(\\chi_A)=1\\land\\forall i\\in A\\;(f(\\chi_{A\\setminus\\{i\\}})=0)\\right).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"B\\in\\mathcal X(f)\\Longleftrightarrow\n\\left(f(\\chi_{[n]\\setminus B})=0\\land\\forall i\\in B\\;(f(\\chi_{([n]\\setminus B)\\cup\\{i\\}})=1)\\right).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[B\\in\\mathcal X(f)\\Longleftrightarrow\n\\left(f(\\chi_{[n]\\setminus B})=0\\land\\forall i\\in B\\;(f(\\chi_{([n]\\setminus B)\\cup\\{i\\}})=1)\\right).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"f\\notin\\mathrm{ReadOnceFunc}_n\\Longleftrightarrow\n\\exists A\\in\\mathcal M(f)\\;\\exists B\\in\\mathcal X(f)\\;(|A\\cap B|\\ge2).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[f\\notin\\mathrm{ReadOnceFunc}_n\\Longleftrightarrow\n\\exists A\\in\\mathcal M(f)\\;\\exists B\\in\\mathcal X(f)\\;(|A\\cap B|\\ge2).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>原书 Theorem 10.9，印刷 p.472／PDF p.496。正性使单点删除检验足以确认素支持，验证两族见证至多需 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"2+|A|+|B|\">\\(2+|A|+|B|\\)</span> 次函数求值。真支持与双对偶支持必相交，故Gurvich条件失效只能交至少两点。常函数一个支持族为空，符合其read-once常量表示。复杂度结论依赖单次求值可多项式完成，不能把任意oracle的代价隐藏为免费。</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"27-df-minmaxsupport","status":"resolved","id":"a38b86e606184c7f","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[27-df-minmaxsupport]]","embed":false},{"target":"27-thm-gurvich","status":"resolved","id":"2258152dd7a3f9d8","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[27-thm-gurvich]]","embed":false},{"target":"27-df-minmaxsupport","status":"resolved","id":"a38b86e606184c7f","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$n\\in\\mathbb Z_{\\ge0}$，$f\\in\\mathrm{Monotone}_n$；$\\chi_S,\\mathcal M(f),\\mathcal X(f)$ 见 [[27-df-minmaxsupport]]，$\\mathrm{ReadOnceFunc}_n$ 与 Gurvich 判据见 [[27-thm-gurvich]]。$A,B\\subseteq[n]$。","embed":false},{"target":"27-thm-gurvich","status":"resolved","id":"2258152dd7a3f9d8","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$n\\in\\mathbb Z_{\\ge0}$，$f\\in\\mathrm{Monotone}_n$；$\\chi_S,\\mathcal M(f),\\mathcal X(f)$ 见 [[27-df-minmaxsupport]]，$\\mathrm{ReadOnceFunc}_n$ 与 Gurvich 判据见 [[27-thm-gurvich]]。$A,B\\subseteq[n]$。","embed":false}],"attachments":[],"math":[{"tex":"n\\in\\mathbb Z_{\\ge0}","display":false},{"tex":"f\\in\\mathrm{Monotone}_n","display":false},{"tex":"\\chi_S,\\mathcal M(f),\\mathcal X(f)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ReadOnceFunc}_n","display":false},{"tex":"A,B\\subseteq[n]","display":false},{"tex":"A\\in\\mathcal M(f)\\Longleftrightarrow\n\\left(f(\\chi_A)=1\\land\\forall i\\in A\\;(f(\\chi_{A\\setminus\\{i\\}})=0)\\right).","display":true},{"tex":"B\\in\\mathcal X(f)\\Longleftrightarrow\n\\left(f(\\chi_{[n]\\setminus B})=0\\land\\forall i\\in B\\;(f(\\chi_{([n]\\setminus B)\\cup\\{i\\}})=1)\\right).","display":true},{"tex":"f\\notin\\mathrm{ReadOnceFunc}_n\\Longleftrightarrow\n\\exists A\\in\\mathcal M(f)\\;\\exists B\\in\\mathcal X(f)\\;(|A\\cap B|\\ge2).","display":true},{"tex":"2+|A|+|B|","display":false}],"bytes":1874,"backlinks":[{"id":"5244dbb38da17b8a","anchor":"ref-101","locations":["正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"[[27-thm-readoncecertificate|thm-readoncecertificate — A pair of prime supports certifies failure of positive read-once]]"}],"outgoing":["a38b86e606184c7f","2258152dd7a3f9d8"]}